  eprint  = {2410.03494},
  archivePrefix = {arXiv},
  url     = {https://github.com/wenhao-gao/synformer},
  note    = {SynFormer: a transformer + diffusion-based building-block selector that generates
             molecules AS SYNTHETIC PATHWAYS (postfix notation over reaction templates and
             purchasable blocks), so its output carries a route by construction (has_route=1).
             THE reaction-aware, non-GFN entrant -- the cell docs/LSD_FLOW_BENCHMARK_PLAN.md section
             7 names as the one that would isolate the contribution of the FLOW FIELD from mere
             reaction-grounding, which no ablation on our own generators can do. Oracle-guided
             optimization comes from experiments/graphga_sf_opt.py (a Graph GA proposes, SynFormer
             projects into synthesizable space, the oracle scores) whose Oracle.assign_evaluator seam
             takes our frozen reward directly. Successor to ChemProjector (Luo et al., ICML 2024); both were
             deprecated by their authors in Dec 2025 in favour of PrexSyn (arXiv 2512.00384), which
             is NOT usable here because v1 dropped the property-based queries an oracle-guided run
             needs. NO ENAMINE LICENCE REQUIRED: the preprocessed catalogue (fpindex.pkl, matrix.pkl)
             and the encoder-decoder checkpoint are on HuggingFace at whgao/synformer, which is what
             GraphGA-SF consumes.}
}
